Step 14 - Baseline

- Simple models (Logistic Regression, small Decision Tree)
- Quick check: Do features work?
- Check overfitting (train vs test)
- Get reference metrics (accuracy, recall, AUC)

Step 15 → Improve the SAME models

✔ Tune hyperparameters (regularization, tree depth)
✔ Fix over/underfitting observed in Step 14
✔ Improve recall for churn

Step 16 Advanced models

✔ Random Forest / XGBoost
✔ Capture non-linear patterns
✔ Compare vs baseline (did we really improve?)

1) Debugging clarity
If Logistic already performs well → features are strong ✔
If all models perform poorly → feature/data issue ❌
2) Honest comparison
Baseline AUC = 0.78  
XGBoost AUC = 0.82  

👉 You can prove improvement ✔

If you jump directly to XGBoost:

You don’t know if 0.82 is good or bad ❌

3) Overfitting detection

Simple models make it easy to see:

Train = 0.75, Test = 0.73 → good ✔

Complex models might hide:

Train = 0.95, Test = 0.72 → overfitting ❌

4) Project/storytelling (very important)

Interview or presentation:

✔ Started with baseline
✔ Identified issues
✔ Improved step-by-step
